# Design

## Color architecture
Four roles per palette:

| Role | Usage |
|---|---|
| HERO | Full-bleed backgrounds, 25-35% of page |
| TEXT | Headlines and body, darkest color |
| NEUTRAL | Breathing room, alternating sections |
| ACCENT | Small moments and hovers, 5% max |

Section pattern: HERO → Neutral → HERO → Neutral → Footer

One color dominates. Text color is for reading only. Accents are scalpels, not paintbrushes. One background per section — no color soup.

## Layout
Magazine presentation. Every page is a defined-width content area floating over a muted background (`stone-100`, `neutral-100`). Content has clear edges. The background frames it.

```tsx
<div className="min-h-screen bg-stone-100">
  <div className="max-w-5xl mx-auto bg-white min-h-screen shadow-sm">
    {/* content */}
  </div>
</div>
```

Editorial, not template:
- Asymmetric compositions, not always centered
- Text overlapping images, headlines breaking across boundaries
- Images at varied scale, not equal grids
- Large type with intentional line breaks
- Uneven grids: 5/7 and 4/6 splits
- Color blocking in full solid sections
- Photography carries the page

## Components
**Buttons** — square or minimal radius. Uppercase, letter-spaced, light weight. Arrow shifts right on hover.

**Product cards** — no shadow, no border. The image is the card. Name in small caps below. Price in lighter weight.

**Scroll indicators** — "VIEW MORE" with a down arrow, small caps, `tracking-widest`, subtle bounce.

## Responsive
Mobile first. Design small, enhance upward. Breakpoints are defined in `@theme` (Tailwind v4) — see the stack rules.

```tsx
// correct — scales up
<div className="text-sm md:text-base lg:text-lg xl:text-xl">

// wrong — scales down
<div className="text-2xl md:text-sm">
```

## Anti-patterns
Purple or blue gradients on white. Generic stock photography. Inter everywhere. Too many colors. Too many boxes and borders. Icons on everything. Rounded-everything card grids.

## Accessibility — WCAG 2.2 AA
WCAG 2.2 is the current W3C Recommendation. WCAG 3.0 is still a Working Draft — do not target it.

- Keyboard navigation on every interactive element
- Visible focus states, and focus never obscured by sticky headers or overlays (2.2)
- Interactive targets at least 24×24 CSS px (2.2)
- Any drag interaction has a single-pointer alternative (2.2)
- No cognitive-test authentication — allow paste into password fields (2.2)
- Labels on all form inputs
- Alt text on all images; empty `alt=""` for decorative
- Contrast 4.5:1 body, 3:1 large text and UI components
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`

## Copy
**No hyphens anywhere.** Rewrite to avoid them. Phone: (555) 123 4567, not 555-123-4567.

**Ask for the source URL before writing body copy.** Design is one thing, voice is another. Get the URL so text matches the real brand.

No AI giveaways: "I'd be happy to", "dive into", "it's important to note", "let's explore", "leverage", "utilize", "in order to", "due to the fact that".

Active voice. Sentence case headings. Oxford comma always.
